abstract=(f"Observational studies link higher remnant cholesterol (RC) to non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), yet it remains unclear whether the association is causal, and the two earlier Mendelian randomization (MR) studies reached opposite conclusions. RC is the cholesterol carried by triglyceride-rich lipoprotein remnants, and the liver both secretes these particles and stores the fatty acids from which they are built, so confounding and reverse causation are plausible explanations for the observational findings. MR uses genetic variants as instruments to make causal inferences about an exposure and an outcome. For the exposure, we used 52 independent genome-wide significant variants for RC from a nuclear magnetic resonance GWAS of 115,082 UK Biobank participants (mean F = {S[G]['mean_F']:.0f}; variance explained = {100*S[G]['R2']:.1f}%). We then applied summary statistics from three European-ancestry NAFLD GWAS: an electronic-health-record meta-analysis (8,434 cases and 770,180 controls), the UK Biobank (4,761 cases and 373,227 controls) and FinnGen release 5 (894 cases and 217,898 controls). Genetically predicted RC was not associated with NAFLD in any dataset (inverse variance weighted odds ratio per 1-SD increase = {gi['OR']:.3f}, 95% CI: {gi['lo']:.3f}–{gi['hi']:.3f}, P = {pf(gi['p'])}; {fi['OR']:.3f}, 95% CI: {fi['lo']:.3f}–{fi['hi']:.3f}, P = {pf(fi['p'])}; and {ni['OR']:.3f}, 95% CI: {ni['lo']:.3f}–{ni['hi']:.3f}, P = {pf(ni['p'])}). Heterogeneity was substantial and was driven by a few variants at hepatic lipid loci (TM6SF2, TRIB1, GCKR) [Q~~IVW~~ = {S[G]['Q']:.1f}, P = {pf(S[G]['Q_p'])}; I^^2^^ = {100*het.loc['Ghodsian','I2_IVW']:.1f}%; I^^2^^~~GX~~ = {100*het.loc['Ghodsian','I2_GX']:.1f}% in the first dataset], whereas there was no evidence of directional pleiotropy [MR-Egger intercept = {S[G]['egger_int']:.4f}, P = {pf(S[G]['egger_int_p'])}]. The null result persisted after outlier removal (MR-PRESSO-corrected OR = {pr('Ghodsian')['OR']:.3f}, 95% CI: {pr('Ghodsian')['lo']:.3f}–{pr('Ghodsian')['hi']:.3f}, P = {pf(pr('Ghodsian')['p'])}), Steiger filtering, exclusion of the APOE region, leave-one-out analysis and 11 additional estimator variants, including MR-Lasso, the contamination mixture model, debiased IVW and MR-RAPS. As a positive control, the same instruments were strongly associated with coronary artery disease (OR = {pcR.iloc[0].OR:.3f}, 95% CI: {pcR.iloc[0].OR_lo:.3f}–{pcR.iloc[0].OR_hi:.3f}, P = {pf(pcR.iloc[0].pval)}). The minimum detectable odds ratios with 80% power were {S[G]['mde_or_80pct_power']:.2f}, {S[F]['mde_or_80pct_power']:.2f} and {S[N]['mde_or_80pct_power']:.2f}. We found no evidence that genetically predicted remnant cholesterol causes NAFLD under the current study design; large effects are unlikely in the two larger datasets, but small to moderate effects cannot be excluded.")
