D.figure(FIG+'fig1_study_design.png','Two-sample Mendelian randomization study of remnant cholesterol in relation to non-alcoholic fatty liver disease.','Fifty-two independent variants for remnant cholesterol were harmonised with three NAFLD GWAS. The inverse variance weighted estimator was the primary analysis, followed by pleiotropy-robust and outlier-robust sensitivity analyses. The same instruments were tested against coronary artery disease as a positive control.')
